k / scp/policy-check` traces to D-033 (the rendered Actions check-run name established for the SCP self-dogfood gate). Adopters of the SCP federation primitive enable this required status check on their default branch via `scripts/enable-required-check.sh` from the SCP repo. The script applies branch protection in two API calls (unified PUT for status-checks/admins/reviews + dedicated POST to `required_signatures` sub-resource per the GitHub API shape), refuses to bypass admin enforcement without an explicit `--i-understand-this-bypasses-the-gate` acknowledgement flag, refuses to run in CI (CI=true / GITHUB_ACTIONS=true env-var guards), preserves any pre-existing `required_pull_request_reviews` shape rather than nulling it, and emits an invocation-log block (operator, timestamp, script SHA256 + git SHA, target repo+branch, before/after API JSON) for paste into `docs/reviews/WP-SCP-020/branch-protection-log.md`. The log commit is part of the invocation procedure: an apply without the log entry is considered unrecorded. Estate cascade rollout (WP-SCP-024) drives this script across PIM, recommender, shopify-app, mapp-doc-agent, control-tower; FLA pilot (WP-SCP-020.1) is the canary first invocation | ACCEPTED | Symmetric posture with D-030 (020J `v*` tag-protection), D-031 (020K CODEOWNERS personal-account), D-032 (020D2 SCP-self required-status-check), D-034 (020F `renovate/v*` tag-protection): every operational procedure that mutates third-party repository state ships an idempotent applier + ratifying D-NNN + invocation log convention. The bootstrap-only / no-CI guard reflects that this script writes to a third-party repo's branch protection — an automation tool that ran it unattended could mass-mutate the estate via stolen credentials before any operator noticed. The `--i-understand-this-bypasses-the-gate` confirmation reflects that `--no-enforce-admins` defeats the whole point of the federation primitive on the target repo and so should require explicit intent. The 