 | This is the first slice of WP-SCP-023's implementation chain (023A plan-doc landed at PR #97, commit `7075234`, 2026-05-03 R4 fixpoint). The data shape was specified at plan-doc level; this slice ratifies it as code surface. Default-false on the workflow input is the load-bearing safety property: existing adopters cannot have new behaviour spring on them; opt-in is explicit per invariant 4. The waiver-content exclusion (invariant 2) is enforced by the schema's `additionalProperties: false` constraint on every level + the explicit field enumeration. The MAJOR-pinning posture means schema breakage requires v2.0.0 + adopter migration; v0.1 prefix on `schema_version` reflects the freedom to amend until first adopter opts in. Bus-factor-1 acknowledged: aggregator runs on the SCP repo with single-operator identity (D-031); 2026-07-21 quarterly review covers. Identified at WP-SCP-023 023A plan-doc §9 D-041 reservation |\n| D-042 | 2026-05-03 | Adopt the cross-repo scorecard aggregator pipeline trust model per WP-SCP-023 023C (this PR). Mechanism: per-emit verification via `gh attestation verify --signer-workflow <expected_workflow_ref>` (the GitHub Actions Artifact Attestation OIDC pattern, mandatory per the D-042 reservation note above + 023A R2 MAJ-SAFE-R2-001 closure); index trust rooted in git's required-signed-commits (slice 020J) + `output/scorecards/** @jrnb2024` CODEOWNERS coverage (slice 023A) + branch protection on main (slice 020D2), NOT a separate Ed25519 key layer. The aggregator runs as `.github/workflows/scorecard-aggregator.yml` on a weekly cron (Monday 06:00 UTC) + `workflow_dispatch`; two-job structure (aggregate read-only + commit write-scoped via job-level permissions, mirroring the 023B `attest-scorecard` job split); reads `docs/scorecards/opt-in-registry.yaml` (CODEOWNERS-protected at `docs/scorecards/**`), pulls each adopter's latest green policy-check run's `scorecard-emit.json` artifact, verifies attestation, schema-validates emit, aggregates into `output/scorecards/index.json` (schema: `schemas/scorecard-index.schema.json`), and opens a PR for operator review. Failure modes (verification_failure / unreachable / no_emit) record loudly per-adopter — never silently dropped. NEVER carries waiver content (invariant 2 enforced by schema `additionalProperties: false` at every level). Internal-only workflow per `policies/VERSIONING.md` §\"Scope\" (mirrors 020N conflict-gate.yml posture); no semver bump. Verifies WP-SCP-023 plan-doc invariant 6 (\"Aggregator output is Ed25519-signed\") in spirit — Sigstore/Fulcio uses Ed25519 under the hood, managed by GitHub rather than by an SCP-side private key, eliminating the private-key-distribution surface | ACCEPTED | Symmetric posture with D-041 (per-emit data shape + opt-in model) — D-041 ratified the EMITTER side of the trust model; D-042 ratifies the AGGREGATOR / VERIFIER side. The mandatory `--signer-workflow` constraint was already pre-committed at the D-042 reservation note above (closes 023A R2 MAJ-SAFE-R2-001) — this slice ratifies it as workflow code. The Ed25519-via-Sigstore framing eliminates the chicken-and-egg of \"where does the SCP private key live and how does the aggregator hold it without exposing adopters\" — GitHub manages the keys via OIDC + Sigstore. The two-job permission split (aggregate read-only + commit write-scoped) is identical to 023B's `policy-check` + `attest-scorecard` split (closes the analogous threat surface where workflow-level write permissions could be exploited by a compromised aggregate-side step). Bus-factor-1 acknowledged: aggregator runs on the SCP repo with single-operator identity (D-031); 2026-07-21 quarterly review covers. Identified at WP-SCP-023 023A plan-doc §9 D-042 reservation + 023A R2 MAJ-SAFE-R2-001 closure |\n| D-043 | 2026-05-03 | Adopt the cross-repo scorecard exposure surface — markdown report (`docs/scorecards/<YYYY-MM-DD>.md`) + MCP method `scp.consult_scorecard` — per WP-SCP-023 023D (this PR). Markdown generator at `scripts/generate-scorecard-report.py` produces deterministic golden-file-tested output reading `output/scorecards/index.json`; aggregator workflow `.github/workflows/scorecard-aggregator.yml` extended in the commit job to invoke the generator + add the rendered markdown to the operator-review PR alongside the index. MCP method `scp.consult_scorecard` (registered in `src/standards_control_plane/mcp_server/tools.py`): read-only contract per WP-SCP-023 plan-doc invariant 5; request shape `{repo_filter?, since_emitted_at?}`; response shape excludes waiver content (`reason` / `approved_by` / `waiver_id` — invariant 2) by Pydantic model construction (extra=forbid + explicit field whitelist). The MCP method reads `output/scorecards/index.json` from the SCP repo working copy at call time; staleness is observable via the response's `aggregated_at` field. ADOPT-001 §12.7.15 documents the adopter onboarding workflow. NEVER carries waiver content (invariant 2 enforced by Pydantic models + schema + dedicated pytest scans on both markdown + MCP responses) | ACCEPTED | Symmetric posture with D-041 + D-042 — D-043 ratifies the CONSUMER side: markdown for operators/auditors, MCP for agents/tooling. Read-only contract + Pydantic-enforced field whitelist + golden-file pytest together preserve invariant 2 across both surfaces. The MCP method does NOT introduce a new authentication primitive — it rides on WP-SCP-021's existing Ed25519 receipt mechanism (consult-class semantics). The markdown report is informational and CODEOWNERS-protected via `docs/scorecards/** @jrnb2024`; operators can hand-edit before merging the aggregator PR if needed (regenerator overwrites on next run). Bus-factor-1 acknowledged: the MCP server runs at acc.brokapps.ai; if down, agents lose `consult_scorecard` access but the markdown report + git index remain consultable. Identified at WP-SCP-023 023A plan-doc §9 D-043 reservation |\n| D-044 | 2026-05-09 | Adopt the WP-SCP-024 slice 024B-core operational contracts for cascade scaffolding. Components: (1) `scripts/scaffold-downstream.sh` (`SCP-073-scaffolder` per WP-SCP-020 §11 follow-up + WP-SCP-021 follow-up `SCP-075-scaffolder-compose`) generates adopter-side artefacts mechanically - bootstrap-only (refuses `CI=true` / `GITHUB_ACTIONS=true` per D-035 symmetry); validates `--scp-sha` against SCP main HEAD lineage (warns if not main HEAD; refuses if non-existent); emits a TF-023E-002 warning for post-v1.2.0 SHAs while recommending the v1.0.0 pin; `--scp-sha` 40-char hex regex; `--default-branch` enum {main, master, develop}; `--scorecard-emit` enum; `--output-dir` writability + path-normalised system-path denylist (incl `/private/var/*` macOS canonicalisation); emits `MANIFEST.json` with SHA256 audit; arguments per plan-doc §5.3. Canonical adopter slugs are normalization aids only, not collision-resistant IDs, so cohort repo names must remain unique after canonicalization. (2) `templates/adopter-wrapper.yml.tmpl` is the canonical adopter wrapper shape per ADOPT-001 §12 with Renovate inline-comment marker `# renovate: datasource=github-tags depName=jrnb2024/standards-control-plane-` enabling auto-bump per plan-doc invariant 8 Threshold A criterion; substitutions `{{DEFAULT_BRANCH}}`, `{{SCP_SHA}}`, `{{SCORECARD_EMIT}}`; least-privilege workflow-level permissions (`contents:read` + `statuses:write` only). (3) `scripts/check-invocation-log-entry.sh` CLI tool implements plan-doc invariant 2 cascade-status CI enforcement: 4 enforcement behaviours (fail-closed default for absent/unrecognised; `onboarded` -> log-entry-modified + target-match; `onboarded-operator-bump` -> log entry + `STATUS.md` `TF-024X-renovate-<slug>` row matching invariant 2 regex literally; `blocked-on-adopter-conflict` -> `DISPATCH-NOTE` `TF-024X-conflict-<adopter>` reference + log file NOT modified) + explicit tooling-slice opt-in gate for `cascade-status: not applicable` (`--allow-not-applicable`; default refusal for direct CLI use). Regex via `python3 re.search()` (PCRE-style); exactly-one-match assertions on both `cascade-status` and `**Target:**` extraction close multi-occurrence injection bypasses; adopter-slug canonicalisation per plan-doc spec. CLI tool only - GitHub Actions workflow wiring (`.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml`) defers to slice 024B-extras alongside `enable-required-check.sh --restore` mode + ADOPT-001 §12.8 break-glass procedure. D-044 was reserved for slice 024B at WP-SCP-024 plan-doc 024A merge (PR #102, 2026-05-04); after the operator-decided scope-split (SCOPE-CORRECTION-2026-05-09.md), D-044 stays scoped to core deliverables; sibling D-NNN may be reserved at 024B-extras authoring time for the deferred surface (`--restore` + break-glass + workflow wiring). Slice 024B-core ships under documented protocol deviation per feedback_four_tier_dispatch.md note + justify rule (kernel hook lives in ACC repo only; per-repo install pattern is FUP-ACC-INSTALL-TARGET-REPO-001 - open). | ACCEPTED | D-044 was reserved at WP-SCP-024 plan-doc 024A merge per the §9 reservation block. The original 024B accumulated 7 fix-rounds + 7 R-rounds against a single branch with each round closing 5-6 MAJ but introducing 2-3 new defects in just-added code (R6 missed primary-deliverable workflow wiring; R7 fix introduced bootstrap defect on slice's own PR). Empirical signal: surface area too large (16 files, ~3500 lines added) for single-pass convergence. Operator decided 2026-05-09 to split 024B into 024B-core (this slice; ~5 files; scaffolder + template + CI enforcement script + tests) + 024B-extras (deferred; `--restore` mode + ADOPT-001 §12.8 break-glass + `.github/workflows/` CI wiring + step 7 operator-interactive demo). Split is incremental delivery, NOT descope - both halves still ship; both required before 024C cohort onboarding opens. Original 024B work preserved at `feature/wp-scp-024-024b-extras-parking` branch (audit trail: 7 codex-fix-round-N-audit.log files + 7 R-round archive directories incl r8-archive carry-forward findings). Slice 024B-core scope is internally coherent: scaffolder generates adopter artefacts; CI enforcement script (CLI) validates cascade-status declarations; tests cover both. The CLI script can be invoked manually as a stop-gap until 024B-extras wires it into GitHub Actions. The CLI guard is necessary-but-not-sufficient: workflow-side hardcoding of `--tooling-slice-id` and omission of `--allow-not-applicable` in 024B-extras is the canonical closure path for the operator-supplied not-applicable bypass surface (see FUP-024B-CORE-NOT-APPLICABLE-WORKFLOW-001). Bus-factor-1 acknowledged (D-031); 2026-07-21 quarterly review covers. Identified at WP-SCP-024 plan-doc §9 D-044 reservation |\n| D-047 | 2026-05-10 | Adopt WP-SCP-024 024B-extras operational contracts: `scripts/enable-required-check.sh --restore <pre-state.json>` restores branch protection from the captured prior-state log entry by transforming GET-shape JSON into the PUT body, stripping envelope fields recursively, converting `enforce_admins.enabled` to a boolean, and replaying `required_signatures` through the dedicated sub-resource; restore-mode posture-degradation flags `--i-understand-restore-removes-admin-enforcement`, `--i-understand-restore-removes-required-checks`, `--i-understand-restore-re-enables-force-pushes`, and `--i-understand-restore-re-enables-deletions` are mandatory when the target removes or re-enables those protections; forward-mode now performs a path-pinned workflow lookup for `.github/workflows/policy-check-wrapper.yml`, queries workflow-runs without a branch filter, validates `--expected-wrapper-sha` against actual release tags via `gh api repos/jrnb2024/standards-control-plane-/git/ref/tags/<tag>`, and treats the working-tree diff of `docs/reviews/WP-SCP-020/branch-protection-log.md` as part of prior-entry detection; the new CI workflow `.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml` wires the CLI gate into PR checks with `paths: docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024[C-Z]*/**` plus explicit branch-protection-log.md / STATUS.md triggers and tooling-slice short-circuiting; ADOPT-001 gains §12.8 break-glass procedure and explicitly names the `--i-understand-no-gate-2-verification` escape hatch; STATUS.md and the DISPATCH-NOTE placeholder for the step-7 operator demo are updated in-slice. | ACCEPTED | The 024B split left the restore / break-glass / workflow-integration surface as the deferred half so the review load stayed bounded. This decision ratifies the operational contract that lets operators disable and re-enable the federation primitive safely without widening the adopter-facing API surface, while preserving the bootstrap guard that prevents tooling slices from self-blocking their own PRs. The release-tag SHA requirement is intentionally anchored to actual git tags, not arbitrary commits, so Gate 3 can re-arm against a concrete release artifact rather than against moving main-head. After any break-glass cycle, `prior_restore_evidence_present` scans the full git history, so every subsequent forward-mode re-enable for the same adopter permanently requires `--expected-wrapper-sha` unless the operator deliberately takes the audited Gate 2 bypass; that permanence is intentional. Bus-factor-1 acknowledged: the helper remains operator-run, the escape hatch is explicitly auditable, and the restore demo evidence is still an operator-interactive step outside Codex dispatch. Identified at WP-SCP-024 024B-extras authoring time. |\n\n> D-044 limitation note: the CLI guard is necessary-but-not-sufficient. 024B-extras must hardcode `--tooling-slice-id` per workflow file and omit `--allow-not-applicable` from cohort workflows; that workflow-side hardcoding is the canonical closure path for the operator-supplied not-applicable bypass surface (see FUP-024B-CORE-NOT-APPLICABLE-WORKFLOW-001).\n\n---DISPATCH---\n# DISPATCH-NOTE — WP-SCP-024 slice 024B-extras\n\n**Date:** 2026-05-10\n**Branch:** `feature/wp-scp-024-024b-extras` (off main, after 024B-core merges)\n**Predecessor:** WP-SCP-024 024B-core (merged at 249aa9f). Original 024B work preserved at `feature/wp-scp-024-024b-extras-parking`. Split per `docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-core/SCOPE-CORRECTION-2026-05-09.md`.\n**Successor target:** WP-SCP-024 024C PIM canary cascade.\n**Decision filed:** D-047.\n\n`cascade-status: not applicable` — this slice ships rollback + break-glass + CI wiring; not a cohort cascade slice.\n\n## Backstory\n\n024B-core merged at 249aa9f shipped scaffolder + adopter wrapper template + cascade-status CI enforcement script (CLI) + tests. This slice (024B-extras) ships the deferred deliverables.\n\nCarry-forward findings from extras-parking R8-archive (preserved in `feature/wp-scp-024-024b-extras-parking`):\n- **R8-CORR-001** (extras-parking): cascade-status regex first-match captures trailing inline prose. **CLOSED in 024B-core** via single-pass regex with full-value capture + closed-set validation.\n- **R8-CORR-002** (extras-parking): prior-entry detection runs outside restore-mode guard, emitting spurious contradiction message. **APPLIES TO 024B-EXTRAS** — ensure restore-mode guard scoping is tight.\n- **R8-CORR-003** (extras-parking): TF-ticket match pattern parameterises over canonicalised slug instead of plan-doc §2 invariant 2 literal regex. **CLOSED in 024B-core** (slug canonicalisation now spec-compliant).\n\n## Why\n\n024B-core delivered the WHAT (scaffolder + template + CI script + tests). This slice delivers the HOW (rollback + break-glass + CI integration):\n\n1. **`enable-required-check.sh --restore` mode** proves invariant 7's <30-min rollback SLO is real, not aspirational. Operator-interactive demo at step 7 is merge-blocking AC and is recorded through the placeholder evidence path until the operator completes the real-repo round-trip.\n2. **ADOPT-001 §12.8 break-glass procedure** documents the 3-gate playbook for federation-primitive failure recovery.\n3. **`.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml`** wires the CLI script (shipped in 024B-core) into GitHub Actions so cohort cascade slices 024C–F have automated CI enforcement.\n\nWithout 024B-extras, 024C cannot open. Plan-doc §6 cohort dispatcher precondition: 024C entry gates on BOTH 024B-core + 024B-extras merging + TF-024B-REQCHECK-ENABLE-001 closure (required-status-check `check-invocation-log-entry / check-invocation-log-entry` enabled on SCP main via `gh api PATCH repos/jrnb2024/standards-control-plane-/branches/main/protection`), plus FUP-ACC-INSTALL-TARGET-REPO-001 closure.\n\n## Scope (in)\n\n| Deliverable | Path | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| `enable-required-check.sh --restore` mode | `scripts/enable-required-check.sh` (modify) | New `--restore <pre-state.json>` flag reverses prior branch-protection mutation per plan-doc invariant 7. Existing forward-mode unchanged. **Key behaviours per extras-parking lessons:** (a) GET-shape JSON transformed to PUT-shape via Python helper (strips `_links`, `url`, `checks`, `required_signatures`); (b) `required_signatures` reset via dedicated DELETE/POST sub-resource calls; (c) APPLY_FAIL=0 wrap pattern (failed PUT continues to log emission); (d) posture-degradation flags `--i-understand-restore-removes-admin-enforcement`, `--i-understand-restore-removes-required-checks`, `--i-understand-restore-disables-required-signatures`, `--i-understand-restore-re-enables-force-pushes`, and `--i-understand-restore-re-enables-deletions` required when before-state would remove or re-enable those protections; (e) restore log block captures actual pre-restore state via `gh api -X GET` BEFORE PUT (not just the target good-state). |\n| Forward-mode safety check | `scripts/enable-required-check.sh` (modify) | Refuses forward-mode invocation against repo with no successful `policy-check` workflow run on default branch in last 60 days. **Critical (R8 + R9 lessons):** workflow lookup by `path == \".github/workflows/policy-check-wrapper.yml\"` (NOT by display name); query workflow-runs API WITHOUT `&branch=` filter (PR-triggered runs have head-branch = feature branch, not default; branch filter defeats gate). `--i-understand-this-repo-has-no-prior-green-ci` flag for cold-start. |\n| `--expected-wrapper-sha` flag | `scripts/enable-required-check.sh` (modify) | Validates supplied SHA against actual git tags via `gh api repos/jrnb2024/standards-control-plane-/git/refs/tags/<tag>` (NOT just 40-char shape match). Used by Gate 3 of break-glass. **Mutex with `--i-understand-this-repo-has-no-prior-green-ci`** (R7 SAFE-MAJ-001 closure). |\n| ADOPT-001 §12.8 break-glass procedure | `docs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md` (modify) | New §12.8 (between §12.7.15 and §13). 3-gate playbook: Gate 1 (DISABLE via `--restore` capturing pre-break SHA); Gate 2 (FIX via SHA-pin to last known-good release tag — concrete `gh api .../tags/<tag>` resolution; NOT illustrative); Gate 3 (RE-ENABLE via Renovate-bumped fix release + `--expected-wrapper-sha <release-tag-sha>` REQUIRED — not optional/advisory). SLO <30 min from operator decision to merge-restored state. WARNING + CAUTION callouts for `--i-understand-no-gate-2-verification` escape hatch. |\n| `.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml` | NEW file | CI workflow wiring for the CLI script (shipped in 024B-core). Triggers on `pull_request: [opened, synchronize, reopened]` against main with path filter targeting `docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024[C-Z]*/**` + `docs/reviews/WP-SCP-020/branch-protection-log.md` + `STATUS.md`. **paths: `docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024[C-Z]*/**`** plus explicit `branch-protection-log.md` / `STATUS.md` triggers and job-body short-circuit: if `gh pr diff --name-only` finds no cascade-slice `DISPATCH-NOTE.md`, or the resolved slice is tooling (`024A`, `024B-core`, `024B-extras`, `024G`), the job exits 0 immediately. This closes the bootstrap defect from extras-parking R7 without permitting cohort slices to bypass enforcement. SHA-pinned actions (per D-038 supply-chain hardening). Single job invokes `scripts/check-invocation-log-entry.sh --diff-base origin/main --dispatch-note <found> --status-md STATUS.md --branch-protection-log docs/reviews/WP-SCP-020/branch-protection-log.md`. Required-status-check eligible. |\n| `--restore` mode tests | `tests/check_invocation_log/test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh` (modify) | Add `run_restore_case` + `make_restore_fake_gh` helpers (mirrors extras-parking patterns). Tests: GET→PUT shape transform; APPLY_FAIL pattern (failed PUT still emits log); posture-degradation flag enforcement; `required_signatures` POST + DELETE sub-resource handling; required-signatures removal acknowledgement flag; absolute path normalisation; --expected-wrapper-sha tag-validation (release-tag SHA → exit 0; arbitrary SHA → exit 2); --restore + forward-mode-flag incompatibility (--no-enforce-admins, --plan, --i-understand-this-bypasses-the-gate, --expected-wrapper-sha + --i-understand-this-repo-has-no-prior-green-ci). |\n| D-047 row | `docs/DECISIONS.md` | New decision ratifying --restore mode operational contract + ADOPT-001 §12.8 break-glass procedure + CI workflow wiring. |\n| STATUS.md update | `STATUS.md` | \"Today's chain (2026-05-10 — slice 024B-extras)\" entry. |\n| **Step 7 operator-interactive demo evidence** | `docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/restore-roundtrip-evidence-PLACEHOLDER.md` | **MERGE-BLOCKING.** Operator-interactive after R-fixpoint reached. Real-repo round-trip on throw-away test repo: create test repo → invoke `enable-required-check.sh` forward-mode → capture pre-state → invoke `--restore` mode → verify branch-protection API response matches captured before-state byte-for-byte → commit evidence. NOT a dry-run mock. The placeholder path is the handoff target until the operator completes the demo. Closes plan-doc invariant 7 SLO + 024A R1 MAJ-SAFE-003. |\n\n## Scope (out)\n\n- 024C PIM cascade kickoff. Unblocked when this slice merges + FUP-ACC-INSTALL-TARGET-REPO-001 closes.\n- TF-023E-002 closure. Carry-forward.\n- D-021 May-31 atomic-workday filing. Independent track.\n\n## Carry-forward known findings (from extras-parking r8-archive)\n\nThese were surfaced in extras-parking R8 but not closed at parking time. Address proactively in this slice:\n\n1. **R8-SAFE-001** (extras-parking): `--i-understand-no-gate-2-verification` is a backdoor; D-044 trust-model claim 'Gate 2 wrapper-SHA pin is explicit operator consent' becomes inaccurate when bypassed. Mitigation: WARNING + CAUTION callouts in ADOPT-001 §12.8 + log-block CAUTION line + D-047 rationale acknowledging escape hatch.\n2. **R8-SAFE-002** (extras-parking): Gate 3 forward-mode prior-entry detection misses uncommitted Gate-1 entries. Mitigation: also check working-tree diff via `git diff HEAD branch-protection-log.md`.\n3. **R8 Bootstrap** (extras-parking): workflow self-blocks introducing slice's own PR. **CLOSED in 024B-extras** via paths-ignore `024[AB]*/**` + `STATUS.md` / branch-protection-log ignores + job-body short-circuit on tooling slices or missing cascade-slice DISPATCH-NOTE.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] `--restore` mode logic correct (GET→PUT transform; APPLY_FAIL; posture-degradation flags; required_signatures sub-resource; pre-restore state capture; restore log block).\n- [ ] Forward-mode safety check uses path-pinned workflow lookup (not display name) + no branch filter on workflow-runs API.\n- [ ] `--expected-wrapper-sha` validates against git tags, and Gate 3 requires it when prior restore evidence exists.\n- [ ] ADOPT-001 §12.8 break-glass procedure: 3-gate playbook with REQUIRED (not advisory) prerequisite checks; concrete tag-SHA resolution commands; WARNING + CAUTION callouts for escape hatches.\n- [ ] `.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml` wires CLI script with `paths: 024[C-Z]*/**` + explicit branch-protection-log.md / STATUS.md triggers + SHA-pinned actions.\n- [ ] Tests cover all `--restore` mode behaviours + forward-mode safety check + workflow integration.\n- [ ] D-047 